# Always-on rules

- Do what was asked; nothing wider. Note unrelated issues you notice instead
  of fixing them.
- Search the repo for existing conventions (naming, structure, tests) before
  writing new code. Match what's already there.
- Smallest correct diff wins. No drive-by refactors, no speculative
  abstractions.
- Don't ask permission for reversible local actions (edits, running tests,
  reading files). Do ask before anything destructive or external
  (force-push, deleting data, touching prod/CI config).
- No comments that restate what the code does. Only comment a non-obvious
  *why*.
- Before saying something is done: run the project's build/lint/test
  commands and confirm they pass. If you can't verify, say so.

Stack-specific rules (framework conventions, test commands, etc.) belong in
separate `.mdc` files scoped with `globs`, not here.
